---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Media from '../components/Media.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import { release, site } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="notMyShell">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-meta"><span class="badge">A frontend for your real shell</span><a href="/releases/">{release.latest.tag} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="hero-top">
        <h1 id="hero-title">Your shell.<em>A clearer view.</em></h1>
        <div class="hero-copy"><p class="lead">Keep your terminal. Keep your shell. Get a composer that stays with you, a transcript worth returning to, and a little more context along the way.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/install/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button secondary" href={site.repo}>Explore on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><p class="hero-note">zsh · Bash 4.4+ · Fish &nbsp; / &nbsp; Open source, by raiseCatError</p></div>
      </div>
      <Media id="home-overview" />
    </section>
    <div class="principles"><section><h2>Real shell. Real continuity.</h2><p>Your aliases, environment and working directory belong to a persistent shell session.</p></section><section><h2>More considered interaction.</h2><p>Multiline input, shell-aware suggestions and command feedback, without replacing your tools.</p></section><section><h2>Local, and under your control.</h2><p>No account or telemetry. Configuration changes stay explicit, reviewed and ownership-aware.</p></section></div>
    <section class="section split">
      <div class="split-copy"><span class="eyebrow">01 / A place to compose</span><h2>Think in commands.<br />Not in cramped lines.</h2><p>A persistent editor gives your input its own space. Keep it at the bottom, move it to the top, or let it follow the conversation in Flow.</p><ol class="number-list"><li><div><strong>Write more than one line.</strong><p>Native multiline editing, with Shift+Enter and a Ctrl+J fallback.</p></div></li><li><div><strong>See what the shell knows.</strong><p>Semantic command highlighting and completion without executing unfinished input.</p></div></li></ol><a class="text-link" href="/docs/composer/">Meet the composer <span>→</span></a></div>
      <Media id="composer-input" compact />
    </section>
    <section class="section split reverse">
      <Media id="transcript-history" compact />
      <div class="split-copy"><span class="eyebrow">02 / A record you can use</span><h2>The command ended.<br />Its output still matters.</h2><p>Return to command blocks, fold the long parts, find what you need and copy plain text. Live sessions let a shell keep working after its window closes.</p><p>Actual program output stays actual program output. NMSh adds structure around it, not invented meaning inside it.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/transcript/">Explore the transcript <span>→</span></a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / Make it your environment</span><h2 class="spaced">Useful context.<br />Optional character.</h2></div><p>Route native modules where they make sense. Choose your palette and prompt provider. Keep Vespyr and motion, or choose a quieter view. The frontend adapts; the shell stays the shell.</p></div><div class="feature-row"><h3>Context with boundaries</h3><p>Project, runtime, Git and system facts come from bounded local capabilities. Opening a repository is not permission to execute its code.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/context/">Context Engine <span>→</span></a></div><div class="feature-row"><h3>Appearance with ownership</h3><p>Theme Studio shapes NMSh. Opt-in Theme Bridge can carry that palette to supported tools through reviewed, managed files.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/themes/">Themes and Chroma <span>→</span></a></div><a class="text-link spaced" href="/features/">See the full product <span>→</span></a></section>
    <section class="section split"><div class="split-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Start small</span><h2>One install.<br />Your familiar commands.</h2><p>Homebrew is the recommended macOS path. Source builds are available for macOS, Linux beta and WSL 2, with Node.js 22+.</p><p class="muted">Latest stable: {release.latest.tag}. Verified tap: {release.tapVersion}. The latest release's physical-terminal QA remains pending.</p><a class="text-link" href="/install/">Requirements and installation <span>→</span></a></div><Code code={'brew install raiseCatError/tap/nmsh\nnmsh'} label="macOS / Homebrew" /></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="callout-band"><div><span class="eyebrow">Planned · Future Learn Mode</span><h2 class="spaced">Learn the shell. By using it.</h2><p>A future guide-and-practice experience for Bash and zsh. Real understanding, with isolation that must be proven before real-shell practice is offered.</p></div><a class="button secondary" href="/learn/">Explore the idea <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Read the handbook <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/roadmap/">Follow the roadmap <span>→</span></a></div></section>
  </div>
</Base>
